Make stats' getListElement() return R_NilValue for a list without names
instead of reading off R_NilValue.

getListElement() (src/library/stats/src/optim.c) loops over the names
attribute with STRING_ELT(names, i); under Defn.h that accessor is
unchecked, so when the list has no names it dereferences the payload of
R_NilValue and segfaults.  KalmanLike(), KalmanRun(), KalmanForecast()
and KalmanSmooth() hand a user-supplied 'mod' straight to it:

    KalmanLike(1:5, list(1, 2))
    *** caught segfault *** address 0x30, cause 'invalid permissions'

Return R_NilValue when the names are not a character vector, so the
callers' type checks raise "invalid argument type" as they do for a
named but wrong list.

The upstream PR also adds a regression test (tests/reg-tests-1e.R), not
carried here.  Found by the shared-argument mutation harness, not by a
fuzz target.

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #380, filed 2026-10-15.
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

--- a/src/library/stats/src/optim.c
+++ b/src/library/stats/src/optim.c
@@ -34,6 +34,10 @@ SEXP getListElement(SEXP list, char *str)
     SEXP elmt = R_NilValue, names = getAttrib(list, R_NamesSymbol);
     int i;
 
+    /* an unnamed list has no element called str; STRING_ELT() on the
+       NULL names is unchecked here (Defn.h) and reads off R_NilValue */
+    if (TYPEOF(names) != STRSXP)
+	return R_NilValue;
     for (i = 0; i < length(list); i++)
 	if (strcmp(CHAR(STRING_ELT(names, i)), str) == 0) { /* ASCII only */
 	    elmt = VECTOR_ELT(list, i);
